hadiths[190]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22488","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sulayman, meaning al-Taymi, from Sayyar, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My Lord favored me over the prophets, peace and blessings be upon them - or he said: over the nations - with four things. He said: I was sent to all people, and the whole earth was made for me and my nation a mosque and a purification; wherever prayer overtakes a man of my nation, with him is his mosque and with him is his purification. I was aided with terror for a month's journey, cast into the hearts of my enemies. And spoils were made lawful for us."
"22489","Abdullah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, Mu'tamir narrated to us, from his father, from Sayyar, freedman of the family of Mu'awiyah, with another hadith - and it is said: Sayyar al-Shami. [Compiler remark only; no matn in source.]"
"22490","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ayman, from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Blessedness for whoever saw me and believed in me, and blessedness for whoever believed in me and did not see me, seven times."
"22491","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya and Hammad ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ayman, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it or similar to it."
"22492","Rawh narrated to us, from Hisham, from Wasil, freedman of Abu Uyaynah, from Muhammad ibn Abi Ya'qub, from Raja ibn Haywah, from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) initiated an expedition, so I came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah for me for martyrdom. So he said: O Allah, keep them safe and grant them spoils. So we were kept safe and gained spoils. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) initiated a second expedition, so I came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah for me for martyrdom. So he said: O Allah, keep them safe and grant them spoils. Then he initiated a third expedition, so I came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I came to you twice before this time of mine and asked you to supplicate to Allah for me for martyrdom, but you supplicated to Allah, mighty and majestic, to keep us safe and grant us spoils, so we were kept safe and gained spoils. O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah for me for martyrdom. So he said: O Allah, keep them safe and grant them spoils. So we were kept safe and gained spoils. Then I came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, command me with a deed. He said: Upon you is fasting, for there is nothing like it. So Abu Umamah, nor his wife, nor his servant, was seen except fasting. When smoke was seen in their house in the daytime, it was said: A guest has come to them; a visitor has alighted with them. He remained so as Allah willed. Then I came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, you commanded us with fasting, and I hope Allah has blessed us therein. O Messenger of Allah, command me with another deed. He said: Know that you will not prostrate to Allah a prostration except that Allah raises you a degree thereby and removes from you a sin thereby."
"22493","Rawh narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Ya'qub narrated to us, from Raja ibn Haywah, from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) initiated an expedition, so I came to him. Then he mentioned its meaning, except that he said: Command me with a deed I may take from you by which Allah benefits me. He said: Upon you is fasting."
"22494","Abdullah narrated to us, Fitr ibn Hammad ibn Waqid narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Ya'qub, from Raja ibn Haywah, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it or similar to it."
"22495","Abdullah narrated to us, Fitr ibn Hammad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Malik ibn Dinar say: People say: Malik ibn Dinar - meaning Malik ibn Dinar - is ascetic. The ascetic is only Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, to whom the world came and he left it."
"22496","Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Husayn, from Salim, that Abu Umamah narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever says: Praise be to Allah, the number of what He created, and praise be to Allah filling what He created, and praise be to Allah the number of what is in the heavens and the earth, and praise be to Allah filling what is in the heavens and the earth, and praise be to Allah the number of what His Book has recorded, and praise be to Allah filling what His Book has recorded, and praise be to Allah the number of everything, and praise be to Allah filling everything, and glory be to Allah the like of that - then magnify that."
"22497","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Mashsha - and he is Laqit ibn al-Mashsha - from Abu Umamah, he said: The Hour will not come until the best of the people of Iraq move to Sham, and the worst of the people of Sham move to Iraq. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hold to Sham. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu al-Muthanna is called Laqit, and they say: Ibn al-Muthanna, and Abu al-Muthanna."
"22498","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Zayd, from Abu Sallam, from Abu Umamah, he narrated to him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Read the Quran, for it is an intercessor for its companions on the Day of Resurrection. Read the two radiant ones, al-Baqarah and Al Imran, for they will come on the Day of Resurrection as if they are two clouds, or as if they are two canopies, or as if they are two flocks of birds in rows, arguing on behalf of their people. Then he said: Read al-Baqarah, for taking it is blessing, and leaving it is regret, and the sorcerers cannot handle it."
"22499","Affan narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Zayd, from Abu Sallam, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah said - then he mentioned its meaning. [Matn abbreviated in source; see preceding narration.]"
"22500","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from a shaykh, from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed, so we said: What makes you laugh, O Messenger of Allah? He said: I marvel at a people driven in chains to Paradise."
"22501","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Ya'qub al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Nasr narrating from Raja ibn Haywah from Abu Umamah, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Command me with a deed that will admit me into Paradise. He said: Hold to fasting, for there is no equal to it. Then I came to him a second time, and he said: Hold to fasting."
"22502","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bahir narrated to us, Sayyar narrated to us, that Abu Umamah mentioned that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be in this ummah at the end of time men, or he said: men from this ummah will come out at the end of time, with whips as if they are the tails of cattle; they go out in the morning in the wrath of Allah and return in the evening in His anger."
"22503","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bahir narrated to us, Sayyar narrated to us, he said: Heads were brought from the direction of Iraq and set up at the gate of the mosque, and Abu Umamah came and entered the mosque and prayed two rak'ahs, then went out to them and looked at them and raised his head and said: The worst slain under the shade of the sky, three times, and the best slain under the shade of the sky are those whom they killed, and he said: Dogs of Hell, three times, then he wept, then he turned away from them, and a man said to him: O Abu Umamah, what about this hadith where you said dogs of Hell, is it something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) or something you say by your own opinion. He said: Glory be to Allah, I would indeed be daring; had I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once or twice, until he mentioned seven, I would think I would not forget it. The man said: Why did you weep. He said: Out of mercy for them, or out of compassion for them."
"22504","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, Mu'awiyah, meaning Ibn Salih, narrated to us, from al-Safr ibn Nusayr from Yazid ibn Shurayh from Abu Umamah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Let none of you come to prayer while he is holding back urine, and let him not enter a house except with permission, and let no imam lead a people and single himself out with a supplication to the exclusion of them."
"22505","Abu Ishaq al-Talaqani narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr from Ali ibn Yazid from al-Qasim from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wipes the head of an orphan, wiping it only for Allah, will have good deeds for every hair his hand passed over, and whoever does good to a female orphan or an orphan in his care, I and he will be in Paradise like these two, and he separated between his fingers, the index and the middle."
"22506","Hasan ibn Musa and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Affan said: Abu Ghalib informed us, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from Khaybar with two slave boys, and he gave one of them to Ali ibn Abi Talib and said: Do not strike him, for I have forbidden striking those who pray, and I have seen him praying. Affan said in his hadith: Abu Talib informed us, from Abu Umamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from Khaybar with two slave boys, and Ali said: O Messenger of Allah, give us a servant. He said: Take whichever of them you wish. He said: Choose for me. He said: Take this one, and do not strike him, for I have seen him praying as we returned from Khaybar, and I have forbidden, and he gave Abu Dharr a slave boy and said: Treat him well, so he freed him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What happened to the boy. He said: O Messenger of Allah, you commanded me to treat him well, so I freed him."
"22507","Isma'il ibn Umar narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah from al-Walid ibn Abi Malik from al-Qasim from Abu Umamah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Some of the Muslims grant protection on behalf of all of them."
"22508","Isam ibn Khalid narrated to us, Safwan ibn Amr narrated to me, from Sulaym ibn Amir al-Khabairi and Abu al-Yaman al-Hawzani, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty promised me that He would admit into Paradise from my ummah seventy thousand without reckoning, so Yazid ibn al-Akhnas al-Sulami said: By Allah, those among your ummah are but like the reddish fly among flies. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My Lord Almighty had promised me seventy thousand, along with every thousand seventy thousand, and He added for me three handfuls. He said: How wide is your Basin, O Prophet of Allah. He said: Like what is between Aden and Oman, and wider and wider, gesturing with his hand. He said: In it are two spouts of gold and silver. He said: What is your Basin like, O Prophet of Allah. He said: Whiter than milk, sweeter in taste than honey, and more fragrant than musk; whoever drinks from it will never thirst thereafter, and his face will never turn black ever."
"22509","Struck through. Abdullah said: I found this hadith in my father's book in his handwriting, and it had been struck through, so I thought he had struck it through because it is a mistake; it is only from Zayd from Abu Sallam from Abu Umamah. Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Salamah from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Learn the Quran, for it is an intercessor on the Day of Resurrection. Learn al-Baqarah and Al Imran. Learn the two radiant ones, for they will come on the Day of Resurrection as if they are two clouds, or two canopies, or as if they are two flocks of birds in ranks, pleading on behalf of their companion. Learn al-Baqarah, for learning it is blessing and abandoning it is regret, and the sorcerers cannot bear it."
"22510","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Atish narrated to us, Ja'far, meaning Ibn Sulayman, narrated to us, from Mu'alla, meaning Ibn Ziyad, from Abu Ghalib from Abu Umamah, and Ruh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib from Abu Umamah, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was stoning the Jamarah and said: O Messenger of Allah, which jihad is most beloved to Allah Almighty. He kept silent from him until, when he stoned the second, he confronted him and said: O Messenger of Allah, which jihad is most beloved to Allah Almighty. He kept silent from him, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went on until, when he stood at the third Jamarah, he confronted him and said: O Messenger of Allah, which jihad is most beloved to Allah Almighty. He said: A word of truth spoken to a tyrannical ruler. Muhammad ibn al-Hasan said in his hadith: And al-Hasan used to say: To an unjust ruler."
"22511","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Atish narrated to us, Ja'far, meaning Ibn Sulayman, narrated to us, from Mu'alla, meaning Ibn Ziyad, from Abu Ghalib from Abu Umamah, and Ruh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib from Abu Umamah, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was stoning the Jamarah and said: O Messenger of Allah, which jihad is most beloved to Allah Almighty. He kept silent from him until, when he stoned the second, he confronted him and said: O Messenger of Allah, which jihad is most beloved to Allah Almighty. He kept silent from him, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went on until, when he stood at the third Jamarah, he confronted him and said: O Messenger of Allah, which jihad is most beloved to Allah Almighty. He said: A word of truth spoken to a tyrannical ruler. Muhammad ibn al-Hasan said in his hadith: And al-Hasan used to say: To an unjust ruler."
"22512","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us, from Ma'mar from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Zayd ibn Sallam from his grandfather, he said: I heard Abu Umamah say: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What is sin. He said: If something pricks in your soul, leave it. He said: What is faith. He said: If your evil deed grieves you and your good deed pleases you, then you are a believer."
"22513","Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Isma'il ibn Ubaydullah narrated to me, that Sulayman ibn Habib narrated to them, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The bonds of Islam will surely be undone one by one, and every time a bond is undone, people will cling to the one next to it, and the first of them to be undone is rule, and the last of them is prayer."
"22514","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, Sulaym ibn Amir narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Umamah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressing the people in the Farewell Pilgrimage while he was on al-Jad'a, placing his foot in the stirrup of the saddle, stretching up, saying: Will you not listen. A man from the back of the people said: What are you saying. He said: Worship your Lord, pray your five, fast your month, give the zakah of your wealth, and obey your ruler, you will enter the Paradise of your Lord. I said to him: Since when have you heard this hadith, O Abu Umamah. He said: While I was thirty years old."
"22515","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah from Shahr ibn Hawshab, and Abd al-Wahhab, from Hisham, and Azhar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Umamah the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abd al-Wahhab said: Abu Umamah al-Himsi the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ablution expiates what came before it, then prayer becomes supererogatory. It was said to him: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Yes, more than once, not twice, not three times, not four, not five."
"22516","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar al-Yamami narrated to me, from Shaddad ibn Abdullah from Abu Umamah, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a gathering, and a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred a hadd punishment, so carry out the Book of Allah against me. The prayer was established, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer, and when he finished, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out, and the man followed him, and I followed him, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred a hadd punishment, so carry out the Book of Allah against me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Did you not leave your house, perform ablution and perform it well, and pray with us. The man said: Yes. He said: Then Allah Almighty has forgiven you your hadd, or your sin."
"22517","Abd al-Wahid al-Haddad narrated to us, Shihab ibn Khirash narrated to us, from Hajjaj ibn Dinar from Abu Ghalib from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No people went astray after guidance they were upon except that they were given argumentation, then he recited this verse: They struck it for you only in argument; rather, they are a contentious people."
"22518","Yazid, he is Ibn Harun, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mutarrif informed us, from Abu al-Husayn from Abu Salih al-Ash'ari from Abu Umamah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Fever is from the blast of Hell, so whatever of it afflicts the believer is his share of the Fire."
"22519","Rawh narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abi Abdullah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Zayd ibn Sallam from his grandfather Mamtur from Abu Umamah, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What is faith. He said: If your good deed pleases you and your evil deed grieves you, then you are a believer. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what is sin. He said: If something pricks in your soul, leave it."
"22520","Waki' narrated to us, Ali ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abu al-Muhallab from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr from Ali ibn Yazid from al-Qasim from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most enviable of my allies in my view is a believer of little property, with a share of prayer, who worships his Lord well and is obscure among people, not pointed at with fingers; his death came quickly, his inheritance was little, and those who weep for him were few."
"22521","Waki' narrated to us, Thawr narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan from Abu Umamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he finished his food or his table was lifted, used to say: Praise be to Allah, much, good, blessed in it, not sufficed without, nor bidden farewell, nor dispensed with, our Lord Almighty."
"22522","Waki' narrated to us, Khallad al-Saffar narrated to us, he heard it from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr from Ali ibn Yazid from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sale of singing women is not lawful, nor their purchase, nor trade in them, and eating their prices is unlawful."
"22523","Waki' narrated to us, he said: I heard al-A'mash say: It was narrated to me from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is disposed to all traits except treachery and lying."
"22524","Waki' narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Shimr from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Muslim man performs ablution, his sins come out of his hearing and his sight and his hands and his feet, then if he sits, he sits forgiven."
"22525","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: I heard Shu'bah narrating from Qatadah, and Hashim said: Shu'bah narrated to me, Qatadah informed us, he said: I heard Abu al-Ja'd narrating, Hashim said in his hadith: Abu al-Ja'd, a freedman of Banu Dubay'ah, from Abu Umamah, that a man of the people of al-Suffah died and left a dinar, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said of him: A branding. He said: Then another died and left two dinars, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two brandings."
"22526","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shu'bah narrated to me, from Mansur, he said: I heard Salim, Hajjaj said: From Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, Ibn Ja'far said: I heard Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, he said: It was mentioned to me from Abu Umamah, that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him, with her two small boys with her, so he gave her three dates, and she gave each one of them a date. He said: Then one of the two boys wept, so she split it and gave each one half. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Child-bearing, giving birth, merciful to their children; were it not for what they do to their husbands, those of them who pray would enter Paradise."
"22527","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah informed us, from Qatadah from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Abu Umamah al-Himsi, he said: A man of the people of al-Suffah died, and a dinar was found in his waist-wrapper, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A branding. He said: Then another died, and two dinars were found in his waist-wrapper, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two brandings."
"22528","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ma'mar from Qatadah from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Abu Umamah, the like of it."
"22529","Husayn narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: It was narrated from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Abu Umamah, he said: A man of the people of al-Suffah died, and he mentioned the like of it."
"22530","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ya'la ibn Ata informed us, that he heard a shaykh of the people of Damascus, that he heard Abu Umamah al-Bahili say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he entered night prayer, would say takbir three times and tasbih three times and tahlil three times, then he would say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from Satan the accursed, from his madness and his blowing and his association."
"22531","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ya'la ibn Ata narrated to us, from a shaykh of the people of Damascus from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Five, excellent, excellent: glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest, and a righteous child who dies for a man so he seeks reward for him."
"22532","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata from a man who narrated to him, that he heard Abu Umamah al-Bahili say: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stood for prayer, would say takbir three times, then say: There is no god but Allah, three times, and glory be to Allah and praise Him, three times, then say: I seek refuge in You from Satan the accursed, from his madness and his blowing and his spittle."
"22533","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman of the people of Hims, of Banu al-Ad'da of Kindah, he said: I heard Abu Umamah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning a man who died and left a dinar or two dinars, meaning he said of him: A branding, or two brandings."
"22534","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Abu al-Anbas from Abu al-Adabbas from Abu Marzuq from Abu Ghalib from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us while leaning on a staff, so we stood for him, and he said: Do not stand as the non-Arabs stand, glorifying one another. He said: It was as if we wished he would supplicate to Allah for us, so he said: O Allah, forgive us and have mercy on us and be pleased with us and accept from us and admit us into Paradise and save us from the Fire and set right for us all our affairs. It was as if we wished he would add for us, so he said: I have gathered the matter for you."
"22535","Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Abu, from Abu, from Abu, among them Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it or close to it."
"22536","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, he said: I heard Abu Ghalib say: When the heads of al-Azariqah were brought and set up on the steps of Damascus, Abu Umamah came, and when he saw them his eyes shed tears, and he said: Dogs of Hell, three times; these are the worst slain killed under the surface of the sky, and the best slain killed under the surface of the sky are those whom these killed. He said: I said: What is with you, your eyes shed tears. He said: Out of mercy for them; they were of the people of Islam. He said: We said: By your own opinion did you say, these are dogs of Hell, or something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Indeed I would be daring; rather I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than once, not twice, not three times. He said: And he counted several times."
"22537","Hajjaj narrated to us, Hariz ibn Uthman informed us, Sulaym ibn Amir narrated to me, from Abu Ghalib from Abu Umamah, he said: Barley bread would not be left over from the household of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"22538","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd from Abu Talib al-Duba'i from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That I remember Allah Almighty from sunrise, saying takbir and tahlil and tasbih, is more beloved to me than to free four from the offspring of Isma'il, and that I remember Allah from the Asr prayer until the sun sets is more beloved to me than to free such and such from the offspring of Isma'il."
"22539","Al-Hasan ibn Sawwar narrated to us, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, that Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to him, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun will draw near on the Day of Resurrection to the measure of a mile, and its heat will be increased such and such; vermin will boil from it as pots boil; they will sweat in it according to their sins; among them are those whom it reaches to their ankles, and among them are those whom it reaches to their shanks, and among them are those whom it reaches to their waists, and among them are those whom sweat bridles."
"22540","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr from Ali ibn Yazid from al-Qasim from Abu Umamah, he said: When Umm Kulthum, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), was placed in the grave, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: From it We created you, and into it We shall return you, and from it We shall bring you out another time. He said: Then I do not know whether he said: In the name of Allah, and in the cause of Allah, and upon the religion of the Messenger of Allah, or not. When he built her lahd over her, he began throwing the clods to them, saying: Fill the gaps between the bricks. Then he said: Indeed this is nothing, but it comforts the soul of the living."
"22541","Nuh ibn Maymun narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman said: He is Abu Muhammad ibn Nuh, and he is the struck-out Abu Muhammad ibn Nuh. Abu Khuraym, Uqbah ibn Abi al-Sahba, narrated to us, Abu Ghalib al-Rasibi narrated to me, that he met Abu Umamah at Hims and asked him about things; he narrated to them that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no Muslim servant who hears the call to prayer and stands to his ablution except that he is forgiven with the first drop that touches his palm of that water; by the number of those drops until he finishes his ablution, except that he is forgiven what preceded of his sins, and he stands to his prayer while it is supererogatory. Abu Ghalib said: I said to Abu Umamah: Did you hear this from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Yes, by the One who sent him with the truth as a bringer of glad tidings and a warner, more than once, not twice, not three, not four, not five, not six, not seven, not eight, not nine, not ten, and ten, and ten, and he clapped with his hands."
"22542","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr from Ali ibn Yazid from al-Qasim from Abu Umamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying and said: Will no man give charity to this one and pray with him. A man stood and prayed with him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These two are a congregation."
"22543","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Zahr narrated to us, from Ali ibn Yazid from al-Qasim from Abu Umamah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: And it was narrated to us with this chain from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: My Lord Almighty offered me to make the valley of Makkah gold for me, so I said: No, O Lord, but I am full one day and hungry one day, or the like of that; when I am hungry I humble myself to You and remember You, and when I am full I praise You and thank You."
"22544","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak informed us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr from Ali ibn Yazid from al-Qasim from Abu Umamah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah Almighty said: The most beloved thing by which My servant worships Me is sincerity to Me."
"22545","Attab, and he is Ibn Ziyad, narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr from Ali ibn Yazid from al-Qasim from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever begins with greeting is most deserving of Allah Almighty and His Messenger."
"22546","Affan narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Zayd from Abu Sallam from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite the Quran, for it will come as an intercessor on the Day of Resurrection for its companion. Recite the two radiant ones, al-Baqarah and Al Imran, for they will come on the Day of Resurrection as if they are two canopies, or as if they are two clouds, or as if they are two flocks of birds in ranks, pleading on behalf of their companions. Recite Surah al-Baqarah, for taking it is blessing and leaving it is regret, and the sorcerers cannot bear it."
"22547","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Abu Talib al-Duba'i from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That I sit remembering Allah, and saying takbir of Him and praising Him and glorifying Him and declaring His oneness, until the sun rises, is more beloved to me than to free two necks, or more, from the offspring of Isma'il, and from after Asr until the sun sets is more beloved to me than to free four necks from the offspring of Isma'il."
"22548","Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us, and Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Ya'qub al-Dabbi narrated to us, from Raja ibn Haywah from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) launched a raid, so I came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah for me for martyrdom. He said: O Allah, keep them safe and grant them spoils. He said: So we raided, and we were safe and gained spoils. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) launched a second raid, so I came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah for me for martyrdom. He said: O Allah, keep them safe and grant them spoils. He said: So we raided, and we were safe and gained spoils. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) launched a third raid, so I came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I came to you successively twice asking you to supplicate to Allah for me for martyrdom, and you said: O Allah, keep them safe and grant them spoils. O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah for me for martyrdom. He said: O Allah, keep them safe and grant them spoils. He said: So we raided, and we were safe and gained spoils. Then I came to him after that and said: O Messenger of Allah, command me with a deed I may take from you by which Allah will benefit me. He said: Hold to fasting, for there is no like to it. He said: Abu Umamah and his wife and his servant would not be found except fasting; if they saw fire or smoke in the daytime in their house, they knew a guest had come upon them. He said: Then I came to him after, and said: O Messenger of Allah, you commanded me with a matter, and I hope Allah Almighty has benefited me by it, so command me with another matter by which Allah will benefit me. He said: Know that you do not prostrate to Allah a prostration except that Allah raises you a degree by it, or removes, or he said: and removes, Mahdi doubted, from you by it a sin."
"22549","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Salim ibn Hayyan informed us, Abu Ghalib narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Umamah say: If you place purification in its places, you sit forgiven; if he stands and prays, it is merit and reward for him, and if he sits, he sits forgiven. A man said to him: O Abu Umamah, what if he stands and prays, will it be supererogatory for him. He said: No, supererogatory is only for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); how can it be supererogatory for him while he strives in sins and errors; it will be merit and reward for him."
"22550","Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Layth ibn Abi Sulaym informed us, from Ubaydullah from al-Qasim from Abu Umamah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The most enviable of people in my view is a believing servant of little property, with a share of prayer, who obeyed his Lord and worshipped Him well in secret, and was obscure among people, not pointed at with fingers, and whose livelihood was sufficiency, and whose livelihood was sufficiency. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made tapping with his fingers, and whose livelihood was sufficiency, and whose livelihood was sufficiency, then his death came quickly, and those who wept for him were few, and his inheritance was little. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I asked my father, I said: What is his inheritance. He said: His legacy."
"22551","Aswad narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abu al-Muhallab from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr from Ali ibn Yazid, and he mentioned the hadith, and he tapped with his hand."
"22552","Isma'il narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Zayd ibn Sallam from his grandfather Mamtur from Abu Umamah, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, what is faith. He said: If your good deed pleases you and your evil deed grieves you, then you are a believer. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what is sin. He said: If something pricks in your chest, leave it."
"22553","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Thawr from Khalid ibn Ma'dan from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when the table was lifted, used to say: Praise be to Allah, much, good, blessed in it, not sufficed without, nor bidden farewell, nor dispensed with, our Lord."
"22554","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Mis'ar, Abu al-Adabbas narrated to us, from a man, I think him Abu Khalaf, Abu Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Abu Umamah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us, and when we saw him we stood. He said: When you see me, do not stand as the non-Arabs do, glorifying one another. He said: It was as if we wished he would supplicate for us, so he said: O Allah, forgive us and have mercy on us and be pleased with us and accept from us and admit us into Paradise and save us from the Fire and set right for us all our affairs."
"22555","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Husayn al-Khurasani from Abu Ghalib from Abu Umamah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah Almighty has at every breaking of fast those freed. Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I heard my father say: This Husayn al-Khurasani, he is Husayn ibn Waqid."
"22556","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Husayn al-Khurasani from Abu Ghalib from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed one day, and it was said to him: O Messenger of Allah, what made you laugh. He said: People driven to Paradise bound together in chains."
"22557","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Dinar al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No people went astray after guidance they were upon except that they were given argumentation, then he recited: They struck it for you only in argument; rather, they are a contentious people."
"22558","Ya'la narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, the like of it."
"22559","Waki' narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Shimr from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Muslim man performs ablution, his sins come out of his hearing and his sight and his hands and his feet, then if he sits, he sits forgiven."
"22560","Waki' narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib from Abu Umamah, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at the first Jamarah and said: O Messenger of Allah, which jihad is best. He kept silent from him and did not answer him. Then he asked him at the second Jamarah, and he said to him the like of that. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned the Jamarah of al-Aqabah and placed his foot in the stirrup, he said: Where is the questioner. He said: A word of justice before a tyrannical ruler."
"22561","Waki' narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib from Abu Umamah, that he saw heads set up on the steps of the mosque of Damascus, so Abu Umamah said: Dogs of Hell, dogs of Hell, three times; the worst slain under the surface of the sky; the best slain are those whom they killed. Then he recited: On the day when faces whiten and faces blacken, the two verses. I said to Abu Umamah: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Had I not heard it except twice or three or four or five or six or seven times, I would not have narrated it to you."
"22562","Yazid narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Sayyar from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was favored with four: the earth was made for my ummah a mosque and a purification, and I was sent to all people, and I was aided with terror from a month's journey going before me, and spoils were made lawful for my ummah."
"22563","Waki' narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Shimr ibn Atiyyah from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Abu Umamah: As supererogatory for you. He said: Supererogatory was only particular to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"22564","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hariz narrated to us, Sulaym ibn Amir narrated to us, from Abu Umamah, he said: A young man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, permit me fornication. The people turned to him and rebuked him, saying: Stop, stop. He said: Bring him near. He drew near to him. He said: So he sat. He said: Would you like it for your mother. He said: No, by Allah, may Allah make me ransom for you. He said: Nor do people like it for their mothers. He said: Would you like it for your daughter. He said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, may Allah make me ransom for you. He said: Nor do people like it for their daughters. He said: Would you like it for your sister. He said: No, by Allah, may Allah make me ransom for you. He said: Nor do people like it for their sisters. He said: Would you like it for your paternal aunt. He said: No, by Allah, may Allah make me ransom for you. He said: Nor do people like it for their paternal aunts. He said: Would you like it for your maternal aunt. He said: No, by Allah, may Allah make me ransom for you. He said: Nor do people like it for their maternal aunts. He said: So he placed his hand on him and said: O Allah, forgive his sin and purify his heart and fortify his chastity. After that, the young man would not turn to anything."
"22565","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, Sulaym ibn Amir narrated to me, that Abu Umamah narrated to him, that a young slave boy came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned it."
"22566","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Yahya from Zayd ibn Sallam from Abu Sallam, that he heard Abu Umamah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite the Quran, for it will come as an intercessor for its companions on the Day of Resurrection. Recite the two radiant ones, al-Baqarah and Al Imran, for they will come on the Day of Resurrection as if they are two clouds, or two canopies, or as if they are two flocks of birds in ranks, pleading on behalf of their companion. And recite Surah al-Baqarah, for taking it is blessing and leaving it is regret, and the sorcerers cannot bear it. Abdullah said: Yazid ibn Harun dictated this hadith at Wasit."
"22567","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, from Qatadah from Ayman from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glad tidings for whoever saw me and believed in me, and glad tidings seven times for whoever did not see me and believed in me."
"22568","Yazid narrated to us, Hariz ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Maysarah from Abu Umamah, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will surely enter Paradise through the intercession of a man who is not a prophet, the like of the two tribes, or the like of one of the two tribes, Rabi'ah and Mudar. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, what is Rabi'ah apart from Mudar. He said: I only say what I am made to say."
"22569","Isam ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hariz narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Maysarah, he said: I heard Abu Umamah, and he mentioned the like of it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"22570","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Amr ibn Dinar from Sumay' from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and washed his hands three times three times, and rinsed his mouth and sniffed water three times three times, and performed ablution three times three times."
"22571","Yazid narrated to us, Faraj ibn Fadalah al-Himsi informed us, from Ali ibn Yazid from al-Qasim from Abu Umamah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah Almighty sent me as mercy and guidance for the worlds, and commanded me to wipe out wind instruments and al-kabarat, meaning lutes, and stringed instruments, and idols that were worshipped in the pre-Islamic age. My Lord Almighty swore by His might: No servant of My servants drinks a sip of wine except that I give him in its place of the boiling water of Hell, punished or forgiven, and he does not give it to a small child to drink except that I give him in its place of the boiling water of Hell, punished or forgiven, and no servant of My servants leaves it out of fear of Me except that I give it to him from the enclosure of sanctity. Their sale is not lawful, nor their purchase, nor teaching them, nor trade in them, and their prices are unlawful, for the singing women. Yazid said: al-kabarat are lutes."
"22572","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Mansur from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd from Abu Umamah, he said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a boy of hers she was carrying, and another in her hand, and I do not know except that he said: While she was pregnant, and she did not ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for anything that day except that he gave it to her. Then he said: Child-bearing, giving birth, merciful to their children; were it not for what they do toward their husbands, those of them who pray would enter Paradise."
"22573","Yazid informed us, Mahdi ibn Maymun informed us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Ya'qub from Raja ibn Haywah from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) launched a raid, so I came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah for me for martyrdom. He said: O Allah, keep them safe and grant them spoils. So we raided, and we were safe and gained spoils. Then he launched another raid, so I came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah for me for martyrdom. He said: O Allah, keep them safe and grant them spoils. So we raided, and we were safe and gained spoils. Then he launched another raid, so I came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I came to you successively three times asking you to supplicate to Allah for me for martyrdom, and you said: O Allah, keep them safe and grant them spoils. So we raided, and we were safe and gained spoils. So command me, O Messenger of Allah, with a matter by which Allah will benefit me. He said: Hold to fasting, for there is no like to it. He said: Abu Umamah would hardly ever have smoke seen in his house in the daytime, and if smoke was seen in the daytime, they knew a guest had come upon them, because of how he and his family fasted. He said: So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, you commanded me with a matter, and I hope Allah has benefited me by it, so command me with another matter. He said: Know that you do not prostrate to Allah a prostration except that Allah raises you a degree by it and removes from you by it a sin."
"22574","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Ad'da, he said: I heard Abu Umamah say: A man died, and they found in his waist-wrapper a dinar or two dinars, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A branding, or two brandings; Abd al-Rahman is the one who doubted."
"22575","Rawh narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman of the people of Hims, of Banu al-Ad'da of Kindah, he said: I heard Abu Umamah, the like of it."
"22576","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Sinan Abu Rabi'ah, the companion of al-Sabiri, narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Abu Umamah, he said: He described the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and mentioned three times three times, and I do not know how he mentioned rinsing the mouth and sniffing water, and he said: And the ears are part of the head. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe the inner corners of the eyes, and he said: With his two fingers, and Hammad showed us, and he wiped his inner eye corners."
"22577","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar informed us, from Sumay' from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would rinse his mouth three times and sniff water three times, and wash his face and his forearms three times three times."
"22578","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr from Ali ibn Yazid from al-Qasim from Abu Umamah from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: You shall straighten the rows, or your faces shall surely be effaced, and you shall surely lower your gazes, or your sights shall surely be snatched away."
"22579","Qutaybah narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal from Ali ibn Khalid, that Abu Umamah al-Bahili passed by Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah, and he asked him about the gentlest word he heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed all of you will enter Paradise except whoever shies away from Allah as the camel shies away from its people."
"22580","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Abu Ghalib informed us, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from Khaybar with two slave boys, so Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Messenger of Allah, give us a servant. He said: Take whichever of them you wish. He said: Choose for me. He said: Take this one, and do not strike him, for I have seen him praying as we returned from Khaybar, and I have forbidden striking those who pray. And he gave Abu Dharr the other boy and said: Treat him well. Then he said: O Abu Dharr, what happened to the boy I gave you. He said: You commanded me to treat him well, so I freed him."
"22581","Ibrahim ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Thabit ibn Ajlan from al-Qasim from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty says: O son of Adam, if I take your two precious ones and you are patient and seek reward at the first shock, I am not pleased for you with a reward less than Paradise."
"22582","Ibrahim ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Yahya ibn al-Harith from al-Qasim from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant loves a servant for Allah Almighty except that his Lord Almighty honors him."
"22583","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, he said: I asked Abu Umamah about the supererogatory, so he said: It was supererogatory for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and for you it is merit."
"22584","Sayyar ibn Hatim narrated to us, Ja'far narrated to us, he said: I came to Farqad one day and found him alone, so I said: O son of the mother of Farqad, I shall surely ask you today about this hadith. I said: Inform me about your saying concerning sinking and pelting, is it something you say yourself or you transmit it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: No, rather I transmit it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: Who narrated it to you. He said: Asim ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to me, from Abu Umamah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"22585","And Qatadah narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab."
"22586","And Ibrahim al-Nakha'i narrated it to me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A party of my ummah will spend the night over eating and drinking and amusement and play, then in the morning they become apes and pigs, and a wind will be sent upon neighborhoods of their neighborhoods and sweep them away as it swept away those before them, because of their deeming wines lawful and their beating drums and their taking singing women."
"22587","Al-Hudhayl ibn Maymun al-Kufi al-Ju'fi narrated to us, he used to sit in the mosque of the city, meaning the city of Abu Ja'far, Abdullah said: This is an old Kufan shaykh, from Muttarih ibn Yazid from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr from Ali ibn Yazid from al-Qasim from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and heard in it a movement before me, so I said: What is this. He said: Bilal. He said: So I went on, and most of the people of Paradise were the poor of the Emigrants and the offspring of the Muslims, and I did not see any fewer than the rich and the women. It was said to me: As for the rich, they are here at the gate, being reckoned and sifted, and as for the women, the two reds distracted them, gold and silk. He said: Then we came out of one of the eight gates of Paradise, and when I was at the gate, I was brought a scale pan and placed in it, and my ummah was placed in a pan, and I outweighed them. Then Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, was brought and placed in a pan, and all my ummah was brought in a pan and placed, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, outweighed. And Umar was brought and placed in a pan, and all my ummah was brought and placed, and Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, outweighed. And my ummah was presented man by man, and they began to pass, and I waited long for Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, then he came after despair, so I said: Abd al-Rahman. He said: By my father and mother, O Messenger of Allah, by the One who sent you with the truth, I did not reach you until I thought I would never see you ever except after grayness. He said: And what is that. He said: Because of my much wealth, I am reckoned and sifted."
"22588","Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Silayhini narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd al-Ansari from Abu Zabyah al-Shami from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Love is in the sky; when Allah loves a servant, He says: I have loved so-and-so, so love him. He said: So love for him descends among the people of the earth."
"22589","Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Silayhini narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman from al-Qasim from Abu Umamah, he said: I was under the mount of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Conquest, and he spoke a good and beautiful saying, and among what he said was: Whoever of the people of the two Books becomes Muslim, he has his reward twice, and he has what we have and upon him is what is upon us, and whoever of the polytheists becomes Muslim, he has his reward, and he has what we have and upon him is what is upon us."
"22590","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr from Ali ibn Yazid from al-Qasim from Abu Umamah, he said: Uqbah ibn Amir said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is salvation. He said: Hold your tongue, and let your house contain you, and weep over your sin."
"22591","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, and Ali ibn Ishaq, Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr from Ali ibn Yazid from al-Qasim from Abu Umamah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Part of the perfection of visiting the sick is that one of you places his hand on his forehead or his hand and asks him how he is, and the perfection of your greetings among you is handshaking."
"22592","Rawh narrated to us, Umar ibn Dharr narrated to us, Abu al-Rasafah, a man of the people of Syria, of Bahilah, a bedouin, narrated to us, from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim man whom a prescribed prayer attends, and he stands and performs ablution and performs it well, and prays and prays well, except that Allah forgives him by it what was between it and the prayer before it of his sins. Then he attends a prescribed prayer and prays and prays well, except that he is forgiven what is between it and the prayer before it of his sins. Then he attends a prescribed prayer and prays and prays well, except that he is forgiven what is between it and the prayer before it of his sins."
"22593","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn, meaning Ibn Waqid, informed me, Abu Ghalib narrated to me, that he heard Abu Umamah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam is a guarantor, and the caller to prayer is entrusted."
"22594","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, Isma'il, meaning Ibn Ja'far, narrated to us, al-Ala informed me, from Ma'bad ibn Ka'b al-Sulami from his brother Abdullah ibn Ka'b from Abu Umamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cuts off the right of a Muslim man by his oath, Allah has thereby made the Fire obligatory for him and forbidden Paradise to him. A man said to him: Even if it is something small, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Even a stick of arak."
"22595","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Ma'bad ibn Ka'b, and he mentioned the like of it, except that he said: From Abu Umamah ibn Sahl, one of Banu Harithah. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is Abu Umamah al-Harithi, and he is not Abu Umamah al-Bahili."
"22596","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, al-Safr ibn Nusayr al-Azdi narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Shurayh al-Hadrami from Abu Umamah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Let none of you come to prayer while he is holding back urine, and let none of you lead and single himself out with supplication to the exclusion of them; whoever does so has betrayed them."
"22597","Zayd narrated to us, Husayn narrated to me, Abu Ghalib narrated to me, Abu Umamah narrated to me, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The angels sit at the gates of the mosques on Friday and write the first and the second and the third, until, when the imam comes out, the scrolls are lifted."
"22598","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, Abu Ghalib narrated to us, that he heard Abu Umamah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Spitting in the mosque is an evil deed, and burying it is a good deed."
"22599","Abu al-Nadr and Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, they said: Hariz narrated to us, Sulaym ibn Amir al-Khabairi narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Umamah say: Barley bread would not be left over from the household of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"22600","Al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr, meaning Ibn Ayyash, narrated to us, from Layth from Ibn Sabit from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not pray at sunrise, for it rises between the two horns of Satan, and every disbeliever prostrates to it, nor at its setting, for it sets between the two horns of Satan, and every disbeliever prostrates to it, nor at midday, for it is at the kindling of Hell."
"22601","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Suhayb, narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray them after the witr while sitting, reciting in them When the earth is shaken and Say: O disbelievers."
"22602","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Luhay'ah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Abi Imran, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Four whose rewards continue for them after death: one stationed on guard in the path of Allah, and one who did a deed whose like of what he did continues to run for him, and a man who gave charity whose reward continues for him as long as it flows, and a man who left a righteous child who supplicates for him."
"22603","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Qasim, freedman of Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Umamah, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not wear silk nor gold. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And I heard it myself from Harun ibn Ma'ruf."
"22604","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Luhay'ah informed me, from Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not wear silk nor gold."
"22605","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Hariz narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Maysarah, who said: I heard Abu Umamah say: A single man who is not a prophet will surely have admitted into Paradise through his intercession the like of the two tribes, or one of the two tribes, Rabi'ah and Mudar. A speaker said: O Messenger of Allah, is not Rabi'ah from Mudar? He said: I only say what I am made to say."
"22606","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Luhay'ah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ja'far narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Abi Imran, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever intercedes for someone with an intercession and he gives him a gift for it and he accepts it, he has approached a great door of usury."
"22607","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, al-Hasan, meaning Ibn Salih, narrated to us, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Ubayd Allah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever begins with the greeting of peace, he is most deserving of Allah and His Messenger."
"22608","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Umamah al-Himsi, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Ablution expiates what came before it, then the prayer becomes supererogatory. He said: So it was said to him: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: Yes, not once, nor twice, nor three times, nor four, nor five."
"22609","Muhammad narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, who said: I heard Abu al-Ja'd narrating from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came upon a storyteller telling stories, so he stopped, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Tell stories, for that I sit from morning until the sun rises is more beloved to me than freeing four slaves, and after Asr until the sun sets is more beloved to me than freeing four slaves."
"22610","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from al-Safr ibn Nusayr, from Yazid ibn Shurayh, that he heard Abu Umamah narrating that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let none of you come to prayer while holding back urine, nor single himself out with something apart from his companions, nor let his eyes enter a house until he seeks permission. Then an elder said when Yazid narrated it to him: We were informed, I heard Abu Umamah narrating this hadith."
"22611","Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah, meaning Ibn Salih, from Amir ibn Jushayb, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, who said: We attended a feast prepared by Abd al-A'la ibn Hilal, and when we finished the food Abu Umamah stood and said: I have stood in this standing place of mine, and I am no orator, nor do I intend a sermon, but I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say at the end of food: Praise be to Allah, much, good, blessed in it, not sufficed without, nor bidden farewell, nor dispensed with. He said: So he kept repeating them to us until we memorized them."
"22612","Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Abu Utbah al-Kindi, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is none of my ummah but I will know him on the Day of Resurrection. They said: O Messenger of Allah, those you have seen and those you have not seen? He said: Those I have seen and those I have not seen, radiant with white marks from the traces of purification."
"22613","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Sulaym ibn Amir al-Kala'i, who said: I heard Abu Umamah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was that day upon al-Jad'a, placing his feet in the stirrup, stretching up to make the people hear, and he said at the top of his voice: Will you not listen? Then a man from among groups of people said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you enjoin upon us? He said: Worship your Lord, pray your five, fast your month, obey those in authority over you, you will enter the Paradise of your Lord. So I said: O Abu Umamah, like whom were you that day? He said: I was that day thirty years old, jostling the camel, pushing it aside for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"22614","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, who said: I heard Abu Umamah narrating from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning His statement, mighty and majestic: As for those in whose hearts is deviation, they follow what is ambiguous in it, he said: They are the Khawarij; and concerning His statement: On the day faces whiten and faces blacken, he said: They are the Khawarij."
"22615","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated to us, Luqman ibn Amir narrated to us, from Abu Umamah, who said: I performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the Farewell Hajj, so he praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: Perhaps you will not see me after this year of yours, perhaps you will not see me after this year of yours, perhaps you will not see me after this year of yours. Then a tall man stood, as if from the men of Shanu'ah, and said: O Prophet of Allah, what then shall we do? He said: Worship your Lord, pray your five, fast your month, perform Hajj to your House, and pay your zakat with your souls content with it, you will enter the Paradise of your Lord, mighty and majestic."
"22616","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Faraj narrated to us, Luqman ibn Amir narrated to us, who said: I heard Abu Umamah say: I said: O Prophet of Allah, what was the first beginning of your affair? He said: The supplication of my father Ibrahim, and the glad tidings of Isa, and my mother saw that a light comes out of her by which the palaces of al-Sham were illuminated."
"22617","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Faraj narrated to us, Luqman narrated to us, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade killing the snakes of houses, except the one with two stripes and the short-tailed one, for they blind the eyes and cause women to miscarry."
"22618","Hashim narrated to us, Faraj narrated to us, Luqman narrated to us, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah and His angels send blessings upon the first row. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and upon the second? He said: Allah and His angels send blessings upon the first row. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and upon the second? He said: And upon the second."
"22619","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Straighten your rows, align your shoulders, be gentle in the hands of your brothers, and close the gaps, for Satan enters among you like the hadhaf, meaning the small young of sheep."
"22620","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Faraj narrated to us, Luqman narrated to us, who said: I heard Abu Umamah say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Close your doors, overturn your vessels, tie your waterskins, and extinguish your lamps, for they will not be permitted to climb over into your houses."
"22621","Abu Nuh Qurad narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I heard my father more than once saying, and Abu Nuh Qurad narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Shaddad ibn Abd Allah, who said: I heard Abu Umamah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: O son of Adam, if you spend good it is better for you, and if you withhold it it is evil for you, and you are not blamed for sufficiency, and begin with those you support, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand."
"22622","Abu Nuh and Abd al-Samad said, Ikrimah narrated to us, and Abu Nuh said: Ikrimah ibn Ammar informed us, from Shaddad ibn Abd Allah, who said: I heard Abu Umamah say: A man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was in the mosque, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred a prescribed penalty, so apply it upon me. He said: So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was silent. Then he returned and said to him another time. Then the prayer was established, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed, then departed. Abu Umamah said: So the man followed him. He said: And I followed him. Abd al-Samad said in his hadith: So I departed with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the man following him, to know what he would say to him. He said: So the man said to him: O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred a prescribed penalty, so apply it upon me. He said: So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Did you not perform ablution before leaving your house and perfect the ablution, then pray with us? He said: Yes indeed. He said: Then Allah has forgiven you your penalty, or your sin, Ikrimah doubted it. Abd al-Samad said in his hadith: So I departed with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the man followed him."
"22623","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, Abu Umamah narrated to me, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Any man who stands for his ablution intending prayer, then washes his hands, his sin descends from his hands with the first drop; then when he rinses his mouth and nose and blows out, his sin descends from his tongue and lips with the first drop; then when he washes his face, his sin descends from his hearing and sight with the first drop; then when he washes his hands to the elbows and his feet to the ankles, he is freed from every sin of his and from every error, like his state the day his mother bore him. He said: Then when he stands for prayer, Allah raises him a degree by it, and if he sits, he sits sound."
"22624","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Mubarak, meaning Ibn Fadalah, narrated to us, Abu Ghalib narrated to me, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The angels sit on the day of Friday at the doors of the mosque, with them the scrolls, writing the people; then when the imam comes out, the scrolls are folded. I said: O Abu Umamah, is there no Friday for one who comes after the imam comes out? He said: Yes indeed, but he is not among those written in the scrolls."
"22625","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Ubayd Allah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Jibril, peace be upon him, never came to me except he commanded me with the toothstick, until I feared I would wear away the front of my mouth."
"22626","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd al-Ansari, from Abu Zabyah, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Affection is from Allah. Sharik said: It is love. And it was cast down from heaven; so when Allah loves a servant, He says to Jibril: I love so-and-so, so Jibril calls out: Allah, mighty and majestic, feels affection, meaning love, for so-and-so, so love him. I think Sharik said: So love for him descends upon the earth. And when He hates a servant, He says to Jibril: I hate so-and-so, so hate him. He said: So Jibril calls out: Your Lord hates so-and-so, so hate him. He said: I think Sharik said: So hatred for him runs upon the earth."
"22627","Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, Sharik informed us, and Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Sharik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from Abu Zabyah, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"22628","Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Aban, meaning Ibn Abd Allah, narrated to us, Abu Muslim narrated to us, who said: I entered upon Abu Umamah while he was delousing himself in the mosque and burying lice in the pebbles, so I said to him: O Abu Umamah, a man narrated to me from you that you said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever performs ablution and perfects the ablution, washing his hands and face and wiping over his head and ears, then stands for the obligatory prayer, Allah forgives him on that day what his feet walked to, his hands grasped, his ears heard, his eyes saw, and his soul spoke of evil. He said: By Allah, I heard it from the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, countless times."
"22629","Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abi al-Atikah, from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A prayer after a prayer. My father said, and others said: After a prayer with no idle talk between them, a book in Illiyyin. Abd Allah said: I said to my father: From where did Muhammad ibn Yazid hear from Uthman ibn Abi al-Atikah? He said: His origin was Syrian; he heard from him in al-Sham."
"22630","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mutarrif Abu Ghassan al-Laythi informed us, from Abu al-Husayn, from Abu Salih al-Ash'ari, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Fever is a blast from Hell, so whatever befalls the believer of it is his portion of Hell."
"22631","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr and Abu Sa'id said, Za'idah narrated to us, Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Umamah, who said: If I had not heard it from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, except seven times, Abu Sa'id said: except seven times, I would not have narrated it. He said: When a man performs ablution as commanded, sin departs from his hearing, sight, hands, and feet."
"22632","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Ya'qub, he heard Abu Nasr, from Abu Umamah, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me of a deed that admits me into Paradise. He said: Upon you is fasting, for it has no equal, or he said: no like for it."
"22633","Abd al-Samad and Affan said, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Ayman, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Blessed is one who saw me, and blessed seven times for one who believed in me and did not see me."
"22634","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, and Attab said, Abd Allah, he is Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: No Muslim looks at the beauties of a woman the first time, then lowers his gaze, but Allah brings about for him worship whose sweetness he finds."
"22635","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Zahr narrated to me, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, raising the hadith, who said: Whoever begins with the greeting of peace, he is most deserving of Allah, mighty and majestic, and His Messenger, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"22636","Abu Salamah narrated to us, Bakr ibn Mudar informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Zahr narrated to me, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not sell singing women, nor buy them, nor teach them, and there is no good in trade in them, and their price is unlawful."
"22637","Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, from Asim, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Umamah, who said: If I had not heard it from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, except seven times, I would not have narrated it. He said: When a man performs ablution as commanded, sin departs from his hearing, sight, hands, and feet."
"22638","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Sinan ibn Rabi'ah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ablution, washing his face three times and his hands three times three times, and wiped his head, and said: The ears are from the head. Hammad said: I do not know whether from the statement of Abu Umamah or from the statement of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to wipe over the two leather socks."
"22639","Zayd ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Ala ibn Zabr narrated to us, al-Qasim narrated to me, who said: I heard Abu Umamah say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out upon a group of elders of the Ansar whose beards were white, and said: O company of Ansar, dye red and yellow and differ from the People of the Book. He said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, the People of the Book wear trousers and do not wear waist-wrappers. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Wear trousers and waist-wrappers and differ from the People of the Book. He said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, the People of the Book wear sandals and do not wear shoes. He said: So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Wear sandals and shoes and differ from the People of the Book. He said: So we said: O Messenger of Allah, the People of the Book trim their goatees and leave their mustaches full. He said: So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Trim your mustaches and leave your goatees full and differ from the People of the Book."
"22640","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Whoever wipes the head of an orphan boy or orphan girl, wiping it only for Allah, for every hair his hand passed over there are good deeds for him; and whoever does good to an orphan girl or orphan boy in his care, I and he will be in Paradise like these two, and he joined his two fingers."
"22641","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abd Allah informed us, Safwan ibn Amr informed us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Busr, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning His statement: And he will be given to drink of festering water which he will sip, he said: It is brought near to him and he loathes it; then when it draws near to him his face is scorched and the skin of his head falls off; and when he drinks it, it cuts his intestines until it comes out from his back. Allah, mighty and majestic, says: And they are given boiling water to drink, so it cuts their intestines. And Allah says: And if they cry for help, they are helped with water like molten metal that scorches the faces, evil the drink."
"22642","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, Abu Ammar Shaddad narrated to me, Abu Umamah narrated to me, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred a prescribed penalty, so apply it upon me. Then he turned away from him. Then he said: I have incurred a prescribed penalty, so apply it upon me. Then he turned away from him. Then he said: O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred a prescribed penalty, so apply it upon me. Then he turned away from him, and the prayer was established. Then when the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave the salutation, he stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred a prescribed penalty, so apply it upon me. Then he said: Did you perform ablution when you came? He said: Yes. Then he said: Did you pray with us when we prayed? He said: Yes. He said: Go, for Allah has pardoned you."
"22643","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Mu'an ibn Rifa'ah narrated to us, Ali ibn Yazid narrated to me, from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while walking in intense heat, the strap of his sandal broke, so a man came to him with a strap and placed it in his sandal. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: If you knew what you carried the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon, you would not have carried the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon what you carried him upon."
"22644","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Mu'an ibn Rifa'ah narrated to us, Ali ibn Yazid narrated to me, from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was sitting in the mosque, and they thought revelation was descending upon him, so they shortened away from him until Abu Dharr came, burst in, came, and sat with him. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, turned to them and said: O Abu Dharr, have you prayed today? He said: No. He said: Stand and pray. Then when he prayed four rak'ahs of Duha, he turned to him and said: O Abu Dharr, seek refuge from the evil of the devils of jinn and men. He said: O Prophet of Allah, are there devils among men? He said: Yes, devils of men and jinn inspire one another with adorned speech as delusion. Then he said: O Abu Dharr, shall I not teach you from the treasure of Paradise? He said: Yes indeed, may Allah make me your ransom. He said: Say: There is no power nor strength except with Allah. He said: So I said: There is no power nor strength except with Allah. He said: Then he fell silent from me, so I found his speech slow. He said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, we were people of ignorance and worshippers of idols, then Allah sent you as a mercy to the worlds; what do you think prayer is? He said: Good placed down, whoever wishes takes little and whoever wishes takes much. He said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, what do you think fasting is? He said: An obligatory duty that suffices. He said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, what do you think charity is? He said: Multiples multiplied, and with Allah is increase. He said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, which charity is best? He said: A secret to a poor one, and effort from one with little. He said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, which of what descended upon you is greatest? He said: Allah, there is no god but He, the Living, the Sustainer, the verse of the Kursi. He said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, which martyrs are best? He said: One whose blood is shed and whose horse is hamstrung. He said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, which necks are best? He said: The most precious in price and most valued to its people. He said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, which of the prophets was first? He said: Adam, peace be upon him. He said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, was Adam a prophet? He said: Yes, a prophet spoken to, Allah created him with His hand, then breathed into him of His spirit, then said to him: O Adam, before. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how many fulfilled the number of prophets? He said: One hundred and twenty-four thousand; the messengers of that, three hundred and fifteen, a great multitude."
"22645","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Mu'an ibn Rifa'ah narrated to us, Ali ibn Yazid narrated to me, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by a man reciting Say: He is Allah, One, and said: It is incumbent, this one, that is, Paradise has become incumbent for him."
"22646","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Mu'an ibn Rifa'ah narrated to us, Ali ibn Yazid narrated to me, al-Qasim, freedman of Banu Yazid, narrated to me, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, who said: When it was the Farewell Hajj, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood, while that day he had al-Fadl ibn Abbas mounted behind him upon a dusky camel, and said: O people, take from knowledge before knowledge is taken away and before knowledge is lifted. And Allah, mighty and majestic, had sent down: O you who believe, do not ask about things which, if made known to you, would trouble you; and if you ask about them while the Quran is being sent down, they will be made known to you; Allah has pardoned them, and Allah is Forgiving, Forbearing. He said: So we had disliked much of asking him, and feared that when Allah sent down to His Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So we brought a Bedouin and bribed him with a cloak. He said: So he wrapped himself in it until I saw the edge of the cloak coming out from his right eyebrow. He said: Then we said to him: Ask the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So he said to him: O Prophet of Allah, how is knowledge lifted from us while among us are the copies of the Quran, and we have learned what is in them and taught our women, offspring, and servants? He said: So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raised his head, while redness of anger had covered his face. He said: So he said: May your mother be bereft of you, these Jews and Christians, among them are the copies of the scriptures, yet they have not come to cling to a letter of what their prophets brought them. Verily, among the going of knowledge is that its bearers go, three times."
"22647","One day we went to a Bedouin, he spread his cloak for our sake and sat long until I saw the edge of the cloak coming out over his right eyebrow; a while later we said to him: Ask the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a question. So he said: O Prophet of Allah, how will knowledge be taken from among us while copies of the Quran are among us, and we have learned its rulings and taught our wives, children, and servants? The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raised his blessed head while redness from anger had covered his blessed face, then said: May your mother weep for you, these Jews and Christians also have copies of the heavenly books, but now they do not cling to a single letter that their prophets brought; know, the lifting of knowledge means the bearers of knowledge are lifted, said three times."
"22648","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Mu'an ibn Rifa'ah narrated to us, Ali ibn Yazid narrated to me, who said: I heard al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman narrating from Abu Umamah, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed on a day of intense heat toward Baqi' al-Gharqad. He said: So the people were walking behind him. He said: Then when he heard the sound of sandals, that weighed upon himself, so he sat until he put them ahead of him, lest anything of pride fall into himself. Then when he passed by Baqi' al-Gharqad, there were two graves in which two men had been buried. He said: So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stopped and said: Whom did you bury here today? They said: O Prophet of Allah, so-and-so and so-and-so. He said: They are now being punished and tried in their graves. They said: O Messenger of Allah, for what is that? He said: As for one of them, he would not keep himself clean from urine, and as for the other, he would go about with talebearing. And he took a moist palm stalk, split it, then placed it upon the two graves. They said: O Prophet of Allah, why did you do it? He said: That it may be lightened for them. They said: O Prophet of Allah, and until when will Allah punish them? He said: An unseen none knows but Allah. He said: Were it not for the tearing of your hearts, or your adding in speech, you would hear what I hear."
"22649","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Mu'an ibn Rifa'ah narrated to us, Ali ibn Yazid narrated to me, from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Umamah, who said: We sat with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he reminded us and softened us, so Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas wept and wept much, and said: Would that I had died. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Sa'd, in my presence do you wish for death? He repeated that three times. Then he said: O Sa'd, if you were created for Paradise, then whatever your life lengthens, or your deed is good, it is better for you."
"22650","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Shurahbil ibn Muslim al-Khawlani narrated to us, who said: I heard Abu Umamah al-Bahili say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in his sermon in the year of the Farewell Hajj: Allah has given every one with a right his right, so there is no bequest for an heir; the child is for the bed and for the adulterer is the stone, and their reckoning is upon Allah; and whoever claims to other than his father or attaches to other than his patrons, upon him is the successive curse of Allah until the Day of Resurrection; a woman spends nothing from her house except with her husband's permission. So it was said: O Messenger of Allah, not even food? He said: That is the best of our wealth. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A loaned item is to be returned, a granted milch animal is to be given back, a debt is to be paid, and the guarantor is liable."
"22651","Abd Allah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to me, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Shurahbil, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: The guarantor is liable."
"22652","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Hariz narrated to us, Sulaym ibn Amir al-Khabairi narrated to us, who said: I heard Abu Umamah al-Bahili say: Barley bread never remained over from the household of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"22653","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Hariz ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Maysarah al-Hadrami narrated to us, who said: I heard Abu Umamah say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: A single man who is not a prophet will surely enter Paradise through his intercession the like of the two tribes, or one of the two tribes, Rabi'ah and Mudar. Then a speaker said: Rabi'ah is but from Mudar. He said: I only say what I say."
"22654","Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Alhani narrated to us, who said: I heard Abu Umamah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, enjoining the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."
"22655","Haywah narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abu Rashid al-Hubrani narrated to me, who said: Abu Umamah al-Bahili took my hand. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took my hand and said to me: O Abu Umamah, among the believers are those whose heart softens toward me."
"22656","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Malik, from Luqman ibn Amir, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: No man takes charge of the affair of ten or more but he will come to Allah, mighty and majestic, bound on the Day of Resurrection, his hand to his neck; his righteousness frees him or his sin destroys him; its beginning is blame, its middle is regret, and its end is disgrace on the Day of Resurrection."
"22657","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Sari ibn Yan'um narrated to us, Amir ibn Jushayb narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Abu Umamah, who said: We were invited to a wedding feast, and he was with us; then when he was full of food, he stood and said: Indeed I do not stand in this standing of mine as an orator; the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he was full of food, said: Praise be to Allah, much, good, blessed in it, not sufficed without, nor dispensed with."
"22658","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd Allah, meaning Ibn Abi Maryam, from Habib ibn Ubayd al-Rahabi, that Abu Umamah entered upon Khalid ibn Yazid, so he threw him a cushion, and Abu Umamah thought it was silk, so he moved away walking backward until he reached the end of the spread, while Khalid was speaking to a man; then he turned to Abu Umamah and said to him: O my brother, what did you think, did you think it was silk? Abu Umamah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: One who hopes for the days of Allah does not enjoy silk. Then Khalid said to him: O Abu Umamah, did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? Then he said: O Allah, forgiveness, did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? Rather we were among a people who neither lied to us nor were belied."
"22659","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: My Lord, mighty and majestic, promised me to admit into Paradise of my ummah seventy thousand without reckoning nor punishment, with every thousand seventy thousand, and three handfuls of the handfuls of my Lord, mighty and majestic."
"22660","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Yahya ibn al-Harith, from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Whoever walks to a prescribed prayer while purified, for him is like the reward of the pilgrim in ihram; and whoever walks to the supererogatory Duha prayer, for him is like the reward of the one performing umrah; and a prayer after a prayer with no idle talk between them, a book in Illiyyin. And Abu Umamah said: Going and returning to these mosques is of jihad in the path of Allah."
"22661","Yazid ibn Abd Rabbih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abi al-Atikah, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from one who saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, going to Mina on the day of Tarwiyah, with Bilal beside him holding a stick with a garment upon it shading the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with it."
"22662","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Bakr ibn Khunays narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Zayd ibn Artah, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No servant is permitted anything better than two rak'ahs he prays; and righteousness is surely scattered above the head of the servant as long as he is in his prayer; and servants do not draw near to Allah the Exalted with the like of what came out of Him, meaning the Quran."
"22663","Al-Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, al-Faraj narrated to us, Ali ibn Yazid narrated to us, from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah sent me as a mercy to the worlds and guidance to the worlds, and my Lord, mighty and majestic, commanded me to efface stringed instruments, flutes, idols, crosses, and the affair of ignorance; and my Lord, mighty and majestic, swore by His might: No servant of My servants drinks a sip of wine but I will give him to drink of festering pus the like of it on the Day of Resurrection, forgiven or punished; and he does not give it to drink to a small weak Muslim child but I will give him to drink of festering pus the like of it on the Day of Resurrection, forgiven or punished; and he does not leave it from fear of Me but I will give him to drink from the holy basins on the Day of Resurrection; and their sale is not lawful, nor their purchase, nor teaching them, nor trade in them, and their price is unlawful, meaning the female players."
"22664","Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Abi Salamah al-Majishun, narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Atiyah ibn Dilaf al-Muzani, I do not know but he narrated it, from Abu Umamah, raising it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: The Beast will come out and mark the people upon their noses, then they will live long among you until a man buys a camel and says: From whom did you buy it? Then he says: I bought it from one of the marked-nosed. And Yunus, meaning Ibn Muhammad, said: Then they will live long among you, and he did not doubt. He said: So he raised it."
"22665","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abd Allah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The visitor of the sick wades in mercy. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, placed his hand upon his thigh, then said: Thus, coming and going. And when he sits with him, mercy covers him."
"22666","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, from Sinan ibn Rabi'ah, from Shahr, meaning Ibn Hawshab, from Abu Umamah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ablution, rinsing his mouth three times, sniffing water three times, washing his face, and he would wipe the inner corners of the eyes; he said: And the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would wipe his head once, and he would say: The ears are from the head."
"22667","Ziyad ibn Abd Allah al-Bakka'i narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Abu Umamah, who said: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with her two sons, while she was pregnant, and she did not ask him that day but he gave her; then he said: Pregnant, bearing, merciful ones, were it not for what they do to their husbands, they would enter Paradise."
"22668","Husayn ibn Muhammad and others said, Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, from Hassan ibn Atiyah, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Modesty and restraint are two branches of faith, and obscenity and eloquence are two branches of hypocrisy."
"22669","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Umarah, meaning Ibn ZadHan, narrated to us, Abu Ghalib narrated to me, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would pray witr with nine until when he grew bulky and his flesh increased, he prayed witr with seven, and prayed two rak'ahs sitting, reciting in them When the earth is shaken and Say: O disbelievers."
"22670","Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, who said: I heard Safwan ibn Sulaym say: Abu Umamah al-Bahili entered Damascus and saw the heads of Harura erected, so he said: Dogs of the Fire, dogs of the Fire, three times; the worst slain under the shade of the sky, the best slain are those they killed. Then he wept. Then a man stood to him and said: O Abu Umamah, is this you say from your opinion or did you hear it? He said: I would then be bold, how could I say this from opinion? He said: I heard it more than once nor twice. He said: So what makes you weep? He said: I weep for their leaving Islam, those who split and made their religion sects."
"22671","Hisham ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from al-Walid ibn Abi Malik, who said: A man entered the mosque and prayed, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Will no man give charity to this one and pray with him? He said: So a man stood and prayed with him. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: These two are a congregation."
"22672","Hisham ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Ubayd Allah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it, and he said: These two are a congregation."
"22673","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, he narrated from Abu al-Muhallab, from Ubayd Allah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Whoever begins with the greeting of peace is most deserving of Allah, mighty and majestic, and His Messenger, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"22674","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Ibn Luhay'ah informed us, from Khalid ibn Abi Imran, from one who narrated to him, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Four whose rewards run for them after death: a man who died stationed on guard in the path of Allah, and a man who taught knowledge whose reward runs for him as long as it is acted upon, and a man who set charity flowing whose reward runs for him as long as it flows, and a man who left a righteous child supplicating for him."
"22675","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Luhay'ah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Abi Imran, from Abu Umamah, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then he mentioned it, except he said: And whoever taught knowledge, there runs for him the like of what he taught."
"22676","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I found in my father's book in his handwriting: Mahdi ibn Ja'far al-Ramli narrated to me, Damrah narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, and his name is Yahya ibn Abi Amr, from Amr ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A party of my ummah will remain upon the truth, apparent, overcoming their enemy; those who oppose them do not harm them except what befalls them of hardship, until the command of Allah comes to them while they are thus. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and where are they? He said: At Bayt al-Maqdis and the environs of Bayt al-Maqdis."
"22677","Abd Allah said: I found in my father's book in his handwriting, and I think I heard it myself from al-Hakam: Al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Muttarih ibn Yazid al-Kinani, from Ubayd Allah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Which charity is best? He said: The shade of a tent in the path of Allah, or the service of a servant in the path of Allah, or the mounting of a stud camel in the path of Allah. End of the hadith of Abu Umamah, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him."
